ng is  you can't just decide to be a knight you  have to be knighted  by another night in a special ceremony  and it's implied that dunk was never  knighted  he tells people that alan knighted him  but it's hinted  that that's a lie dunk always gets  awkward and evasive when people ask him  about his knighting  and he thinks to himself that he's not a  knight  but maybe being a true knight is about  more than a  ceremony the story explores what it  really means to be a hero  dunk heads for a tournament at ashford a  chance to prove himself as a knight  and along the way dunk meets a young boy  he's completely bold and he says his  name  is egg he's confident and cheeky and  asks dunk to take him to the tourney as  his squire  dunk refuses at first so egg just  follows him  until dunk accepts they've got sort of a  shrek and donkey odd couple dynamic  where they annoy each other at first but  gradually become  unlikely best friends the tournament  is full of excitement and splendor  colorful  tents and banners merchants and  entertainers famous lords and knights  warriors from all over westeros come to  joust and fight  lannisters baratheons and tyrells tarlys  freys and dondarrions  and targaryens the hedge night is set  90 years ago when the targaryens still  ruled westeros  so the king is deron targaryen and his  queen  is miriam martel daeron's son and  heir and hand of the king is prince  bailor targaryen  called breakspeare balor is a famous  knight  he's chivalrous wise widely loved and  respected  balor comes to the tournament with his  son vala  and baylor's brother prince micah comes  with his sons  daeron aerion and aegon maika has  another son named aemon but  he doesn't come because he's studying to  be a maester at the citadel  aemon grows up to become maester aemon  jon's mentor at the night's watch  90 years later dunk meets arion  and finds that he's a total [ __ ] he's  rude  cruel vain think like joffrey but with  better hair  dunk also learns that daeron and aegon  are missing  apparently they've run off somewhere  dunk  wanders the tournament and he gets a  crush on a girl called tanzel who works  a puppet show  he hires her to paint a sigil on his  shield to represent himself  as a knight he chooses an elm tree with  a shooting star  cause dunk saw a shooting star at camp  the other night  and instead of calling himself sir dunk  he invents the name  sir duncan the tall so dunk creates an  identity for himself  as a knight but what kind of knight is  he  is he cruel and vain like arion or a  chivalrous like bailor breaks beer  what does it really mean to be a hero  that night prince arion attacks the  puppet girl tanzel  cause tanzel performed a puppet show  about a dragon being slain  and arion considers himself a targaryen  dragon so he gets offended and starts  breaking  tanzel's fingers so dunk instinctively  runs in  and beats up arion to defend this damsel  in distress  it's the right thing to do but it's also  a foolish thing to do  westeros is unfair and hedge knights are  not allowed to hit  royal princes dunk could be punished  with death  so is this heroism or stupidity  in tanzel's puppet show she says all men  are fools  and all men are knights it means we all  have some desire to be a romantic hero  to save maidens and fight dragons and  that feeling is  ridiculous and foolish but it's also  part of what makes us  human arion almost has dunk killed on  the spot  but he's saved by egg it turns out that  egg is  not some random peasant he's actually  prince  aegon targaryen son of prince micah  and grandson of the king egg explains  that his father micah wanted daeron to  write in the tournament with egg as his  squire  but daeron hates riding and fighting so  instead he ran off and got drunk  and he shaved eggs head to hide his  silvery gold blonde hair  which is famously a feature of  targaryens  egg says daeron didn't need to shave  because he just has brown hair  he also mentions that their uncle baelor  also has  dark hair instead of blonde because of  his dornish mother  all this talk about targaryen hair color  might be a hint  supporting the theory that jon snow is  the son of rhaegar targaryen and lyanna  stark  the story is showing us that not all  targaryens are blonde  so jon snow could be rhaegar targaryen's  son  but still have the dark hair of his  mother lyanna  so anyway deyron went on a bender but  egg still wanted to be a squire at the  tournament and that's why he attached  himself to dunk  egg apologizes for lying about his  identity but dunk forgives him because  he also lied to get what he wanted  implying that dunk lied to become a  knight  just like egg lied to become a squire  egg points out that he and dunk  are both from king's landing even though  donk is from the slums of flea bottom  while prince aegon is from the palace on  the hill  so the story often explores dunk and  eggs different perspectives from their  different social classes  arion demands that dunk be punished so  dunk asks for a trial by combat  and arion raises the stakes demanding a  trial of seven  a trial of seven is a fight of seven men  against seven so duncan and arion each  need to find  six allies to fight alongside them this  is  pretty unfair for dunk because prince  aerion can easily get his kingsguard  knights and his father and brother to  fight with him  it's much harder for dunk to find allies  because no one knows who he is  and who would want to risk their life to  fight for a hedge night against  targaryen princes  but dunk and egg do fine to some allies  egg knows one guy and a couple more want  revenge on  arion for being such a prick and this  bloke lionel baratheon signs up purely  for the [ __ ] banter  this is the first trial of seven in a  hundred years and lionel doesn't want to  miss  out lionel is a famous knight he's  called  the laughing storm for his habit of  laughing at his opponents while he beats  [ __ ] out of them  lionel is an ancestor of king bobby b  and gendry and stannis and shireen  and we know from the history book that  years later lionel actually fights  against dunk  but that's another story dunk also  recruits young  raymond fossaway raymond has a falling  out with his cousin stefan cause stefan  betrays  dunk by promising to fight for him then  joining arion  instead cause arion promises to make him  a lord  this creates a split in house fossa way  that still remains to this day  stefan's line are the red apple fossa  ways while raymond's are the green apple  fossa ways  because raymond would rather be an  unripe green apple than a rotten wormy  red one  like stefan so on the morning of the  trial  arion has seven nights but dunk  desperately needs  one more he begs the crowd for a  volunteer  asks are there no true knights among you  because every knight swears an oath to  defend the innocent  but all these knights and higher lords  refuse him  cause the nobility like stefan fossaway  have selfish political reasons to side  with their prince  even when their prince is wrong it's  only a poor low-born man like dunk who  has no political prospects and nothing  to lose  who's willing to fight for what's right  which shows the corruption  and injustice of this feudal class  system  but just when all hope seems lost prince  balor breaks beer  joins dunk he says dunk was a true  knight  to fight against arion so maybe there is  hope  for justice the combat begins and  14 armored knights crash together  dunk gets knocked off his horse and  arion gets the upper hand dunk is not as  skilled or well trained as prince arion  but once they're down in the mud dunk  has the advantage  because donk has experience fighting  dirty on the rough streets of flea  bottom  so he's able to defeat arion and end the  trial  so for a moment it seems that this game  of thrones story has a happy ending  dunk the heroic underdog gets justice  over the shitlord prince but prince  balor  acts all weird 